# meltLinkChecking + meltLinkCheckingRoutes: URL-attribute links compile to the
# type-parameter checkedRouteFor form and are validated with NO given RouteRegistry.

# 1. A valid internal link — /users/{id: Int} matches routes.Routes.user — plus an external
#    https:// link with interpolation, which must NOT be route-checked (stays s"..."). Compiles.
> meltGenerate
$ exists target/out/jvm/scala-3.8.4/link-checking-routes/src_managed/main/melt/components/App.scala
> compile

# 2. Wrong parameter type — {slug: String} against /users/{id: Int} — is a compile error.
$ copy-file changes/App-wrong-type.melt src/main/scala/components/App.melt
> meltGenerate
-> compile

# 3. Unknown path — /admin/{id} is not in the registry — is a compile error.
$ copy-file changes/App-unknown-path.melt src/main/scala/components/App.melt
> meltGenerate
-> compile

# 4. A typo'd link INSIDE a { ...map(i => <a>) } inline-HTML fragment is still route-checked
#    (the flag propagates into nested fragment parsing) — is a compile error.
$ copy-file changes/App-nested-typo.melt src/main/scala/components/App.melt
> meltGenerate
-> compile
